From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:02:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wevtapi: Query, subscribe to, render and format the classic
 event logs.

Everything but a few functions was a stub.  The API now works over the
classic logs advapi32 keeps, as Windows 11 does it (tools/startupgapsprobe
evtapi, evtquery, evtlimits, evtsub, evtrender, evtmsg):

- Queries of channels, files and structured queries with Suppress, with
  the XPath the event log takes: band(), timediff(), !=, positions and
  position(); a position is the element there when compared, only the
  first element is looked at when testing whether there is one; a
  string is compared with a number as one only if it is a number all
  through; at most 24 parentheses, 21 predicates and 23 operands of
  "and" or "or".  Windows' results for a position compared with != < >
  contradict themselves and are not copied.
- Subscriptions: the events there already are there for EvtNext at once
  and do not set the signal, EvtNext never waits, asking again after it
  said there are no more is an invalid operation, the signal is the
  caller's to reset, a callback is called on the subscription's thread.
- Rendering of the event XML and of the system, user and path contexts,
  with Windows' layout: each value's data from the next multiple of 8,
  the strings of a classic event an array (the user context still
  leaves room for its table), the whole buffer cleared, render paths a
  tree in which an element already there cannot be added again.
- Formatting of messages, levels, tasks and keywords in the publisher's
  language or the user's, with the terminators Windows gives each, and
  of the XML with its RenderingInfo; bookmarks, log information,
  clearing and exporting logs, channels and their configuration.

What is not the same: classic records have no process and thread ids,
so Execution has 0 for both; log files are .evt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

